161 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 72 0 R
/E ( Beyond Meat defines itself as a food technology company that changes the way consumers experience protein, offering the taste and texture of meat through plant-based ingredients. Their value proposition is about being able to enjoy the food while making better choices for their health and the planet. Their product also matches real meat protein but contains significantly less fat and no cholesterol. The packaging is created to look like regular meat packaging, and the placement in grocery stores is intended to be in the meat aisle. This positioning strategy is intended to overcome psychological barriers around meat-eating by designing the product and brand experience to feel as familiar as possible. At the same time, the company also keeps the environmental and animal welfare parts of its goal open but not obvious in its advertising to consumers. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
